Property:
	Tag: [Guide, Module]
	Module: Text

The **Text** module draws your writing. Every Markdown paragraph, heading, list item, quote, and table is a block of its own. Back to [[Welcome]].

## Styles

**Bold**, *italic*, ~~strikethrough~~, ==highlight==, `inline code`, and [colored words]{Color: Accent}. A color can be a theme name ([danger]{Color: Danger}, [success]{Color: Success}) or any hex code ([rust]{Color: #b5452c}). Select text for the format bar, or press `Ctrl+B` and `Ctrl+I`.

## Links and tags

- A link to another note: [[Math]], or with a label: [[Chemistry|the chemistry guide]].
- A web link: [octaether.com](https://octaether.com).
- Tags: #Guide and #[Two Words]. In the Read view, a click on a tag searches for it.

## Lists

1. Numbered lists count by themselves.
2. `Enter` continues a list, and `Enter` on an empty item ends it.
- [x] A to-do ticks when you click its box.
- [ ] This one is still open.

## Quotes and tables

> A quote is a block too.
> It can run over several lines.

| Symbol | Name | Value |
|:--|:--:|--:|
| {Math: \pi} | pi | 3.14159 |
| {Math: e} | Euler's number | 2.71828 |

## Pictures

A picture fits in a line: `![what it shows](Octahedron.svg)` as in Markdown, or `![[Octahedron.svg]]` as in Obsidian. The [[Image]] guide shows more.

## Anything in a sentence

Any block type fits in a line of text as `{Type: …}`: water is {Chem: H_2O}, a derivative is {Math: \frac{d}{dx} x^2 = 2x}, and code is {Code {Language: Python}: print("hi")}.

> [!tip] Obsidian callouts
> Notes pasted from Obsidian keep their callouts. The [[Layout]] guide shows Octaether's own.
